`,s.jsx(e.p,{children:"In this example the bundle is a product: position times displacement. That is the simplest case, and it is enough for the local calculations below. In a general bundle, a small neighborhood still looks like a product, but those local descriptions need not fit together as one global product."}),`
`,s.jsx(e.p,{children:"A concrete example is a strip closed into a loop. Join its ends without a flip and a displacement can remain positive all the way around. Join them with a half twist and the same continuous, nonzero choice cannot return to itself: the joining identifies a positive displacement at one end with a negative displacement at the other. This is the line-bundle version of the Möbius strip. The global joining matters even when every small piece looks ordinary."}),`
